(4071511, 568271, 37930, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by magnus:</b></div><hr/><i> Great composition, but the background and foreground really don''t look matched. I think it''s the floor being uniformly blurred that''s bothering me, it should be much more blurred in the distance than near her feet (there''s a way to specify the blur radius as a gradient in PS) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There is no blur on the ice, the shadows just have soft edges... note the scratches in the ice. As far as focus/blur goes this is exactly how it looked out of the camera. I changed <b>alot</b> with colors (mostly on the skater; her gown was not transparent) and contrast but only applied light sharpening an zero blur.</td>', 'Originally posted by magnus: Great composition, but the background and foreground really don''t look matched. I think it''s the floor being uniformly blurred that''s bothering me, it should be much more blurred in the distance than near her feet (there''s a way to specify the blur radius as a gradient in PS)   There is no blur on the ice, the shadows just have soft edges... note the scratches in the ice. As far as focus/blur goes this is exactly how it looked out of the camera. I changed alot with colors (mostly on the skater; her gown was not transparent) and contrast but only applied light sharpening an zero blur.', '2007-09-08 03:02:21.000000', NULL, 0),
