(4071547, 579599, 41337, '<td valign="top">Wow Deb. You got a 10 from me.</td>', 'Wow Deb. You got a 10 from me.', '2007-09-08 03:56:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071551, 579194, 39430, '<td valign="top">I nearly submitted an exact replica to this, but decided against it, based on the assumption there would be too many similar images to compete against.  Congratulations on getting a good score - better than my 2nd choice image scored, but that''s the risk I took.  :)  Well done.</td>', 'I nearly submitted an exact replica to this, but decided against it, based on the assumption there would be too many similar images to compete against.  Congratulations on getting a good score - better than my 2nd choice image scored, but that''s the risk I took.  :)  Well done.', '2007-09-08 04:01:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071555, 568248, 16241, '<td valign="top">excellent, congrats on high finish.</td>', 'excellent, congrats on high finish.', '2007-09-08 04:05:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071559, 568544, 41337, '<td valign="top">Not a bad reproduction. Congrats on your personal best and BIG PROPS for crediting the real author of the idea. I wish more people had your honesty.</td>', 'Not a bad reproduction. Congrats on your personal best and BIG PROPS for crediting the real author of the idea. I wish more people had your honesty.', '2007-09-08 04:07:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071561, 579827, 30861, '<td valign="top">WONDERFUL shot Neal! Beautifully done. But in reference this part of your notes:<br/> <br/>"I would have loved for a train to cross the trestle, but it didn''t happen and this light only lasted a short while. "<br/> <br/>Tsk tsk. This was expert editing. Leave the tripod set up and wait for a train, then bring him in on the dawn shot :-)<br/> <br/></td>', 'WONDERFUL shot Neal! Beautifully done. But in reference this part of your notes: "I would have loved for a train to cross the trestle, but it didn''t happen and this light only lasted a short while. " Tsk tsk. This was expert editing. Leave the tripod set up and wait for a train, then bring him in on the dawn shot :-) ', '2007-09-08 04:09:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071563, 579707, 30861, '<td valign="top">Just gorgeous!</td>', 'Just gorgeous!', '2007-09-08 04:09:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071566, 579073, 62727, '<td valign="top">This is fantastic!!!! I LOVE it!!!!  I missed this one in voting, but you definitely would have gotten a 10 from me.  Congrats on your blue.</td>', 'This is fantastic!!!! I LOVE it!!!!  I missed this one in voting, but you definitely would have gotten a 10 from me.  Congrats on your blue.', '2007-09-08 04:10:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071568, 573599, 41337, '<td valign="top">I almost commented on this during the challenge. The light on the water and the reflections are most beautiful.</td>', 'I almost commented on this during the challenge. The light on the water and the reflections are most beautiful.', '2007-09-08 04:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071569, 579488, 62727, '<td valign="top">This is fabulous!  Congrats on a well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'This is fabulous!  Congrats on a well deserved ribbon!', '2007-09-08 04:12:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071571, 572304, 41337, '<td valign="top">I thought for sure this would be much higher.</td>', 'I thought for sure this would be much higher.', '2007-09-08 04:14:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071572, 566418, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is very interesting, and skilfully done. <br/> <br/>I''m not wild about the gradient on the gray BG; I assume the idea is to present this as if it is a standalone construction, and I find myself wondering how this would have worked if you had exactly duplicated the DPC flat gray, then done something like using that gray for both BG &amp; a border on your image, a pretty wide border, so the whole would float with the DPC-standard black hairlines loosely defining the target space. Or something like that... <br/> <br/>I''d love to see you do a variation and see if it seems more or less 3-D. Regardless, a really crisp image and a fascinating presentation.</td>', 'This is very interesting, and skilfully done.  I''m not wild about the gradient on the gray BG; I assume the idea is to present this as if it is a standalone construction, and I find myself wondering how this would have worked if you had exactly duplicated the DPC flat gray, then done something like using that gray for both BG & a border on your image, a pretty wide border, so the whole would float with the DPC-standard black hairlines loosely defining the target space. Or something like that...  I''d love to see you do a variation and see if it seems more or less 3-D. Regardless, a really crisp image and a fascinating presentation.', '2007-09-08 04:14:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071573, 576480, 62727, '<td valign="top">Oh, wow!  I love this!  Congrats on an excellent score.</td>', 'Oh, wow!  I love this!  Congrats on an excellent score.', '2007-09-08 04:14:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071576, 572878, 41337, '<td valign="top">Wonderful study. Great job!</td>', 'Wonderful study. Great job!', '2007-09-08 04:15:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071577, 579599, 30861, '<td valign="top">really sweet! As a denizen of marshes and other tidal areas, I''ve got to love it.</td>', 'really sweet! As a denizen of marshes and other tidal areas, I''ve got to love it.', '2007-09-08 04:16:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071579, 579827, 62727, '<td valign="top">This is incredible!!!  Missed it during voting, but would have given you a 10!!  WOW!</td>', 'This is incredible!!!  Missed it during voting, but would have given you a 10!!  WOW!', '2007-09-08 04:16:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071580, 571023, 41337, '<td valign="top">Wow that must have been cool to shoot. This is rather underrated, IMO.</td>', 'Wow that must have been cool to shoot. This is rather underrated, IMO.', '2007-09-08 04:16:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071583, 576167, 30861, '<td valign="top">Aside from that this image is powerfully done, all the stuff people notice, let me say that I find the foreground vegetation to be particularly well-balanced in the overall composition, where many might have left it quite dark. It''s a great anchor to the otherwise-symmetricality of the image as a whole. Beautiful!</td>', 'Aside from that this image is powerfully done, all the stuff people notice, let me say that I find the foreground vegetation to be particularly well-balanced in the overall composition, where many might have left it quite dark. It''s a great anchor to the otherwise-symmetricality of the image as a whole. Beautiful!', '2007-09-08 04:18:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071584, 576480, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''m so glad to see this do so well! Terrific image, offbeat and appealing in an almost eerie way.</td>', 'I''m so glad to see this do so well! Terrific image, offbeat and appealing in an almost eerie way.', '2007-09-08 04:19:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071586, 575211, 30861, '<td valign="top">This one appealed to me right from the get-go. The B/W conversion is extremely well done. Fine image and a great finish.</td>', 'This one appealed to me right from the get-go. The B/W conversion is extremely well done. Fine image and a great finish.', '2007-09-08 04:20:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071593, 568544, 30861, '<td valign="top">The Pinedo image immediately came to mind when I saw this entry, and I googled it to see how close they were. At first I was a tad annoyed at such blatant "copying", but then I did a reality check and said to myself, "Hey Ward, we DPCers copy EACH OTHER all the time, in the spirit of learning "how they did that", so why not do the same with an outside-DPC image?"<br/> <br/>And you did it very well indeed, and I am delighted to see you crediting Pinedo in your notes. This is just the way it ought to be.<br/> <br/>The Pinedo image has much more subtle modeling on the umbrellas, and I prefer that, but regardless this is a compelling image; congrats on your top-20!</td>', 'The Pinedo image immediately came to mind when I saw this entry, and I googled it to see how close they were. At first I was a tad annoyed at such blatant "copying", but then I did a reality check and said to myself, "Hey Ward, we DPCers copy EACH OTHER all the time, in the spirit of learning "how they did that", so why not do the same with an outside-DPC image?" And you did it very well indeed, and I am delighted to see you crediting Pinedo in your notes. This is just the way it ought to be. The Pinedo image has much more subtle modeling on the umbrellas, and I prefer that, but regardless this is a compelling image; congrats on your top-20!', '2007-09-08 04:25:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071596, 576942, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''d never have pegged this as yours, Ursula. It''s very well done, and I really appreciate the detailed notes on how you organized it. But you mention putting in the skyline in two different steps, so I am wondering if it''s a typo in step 2?<br/> <br/>Congrats on top-20!</td>', 'I''d never have pegged this as yours, Ursula. It''s very well done, and I really appreciate the detailed notes on how you organized it. But you mention putting in the skyline in two different steps, so I am wondering if it''s a typo in step 2? Congrats on top-20!', '2007-09-08 04:28:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071598, 579181, 30861, '<td valign="top">That''s quite an interesting use of "flood" :-) Congrats on top-20!</td>', 'That''s quite an interesting use of "flood" :-) Congrats on top-20!', '2007-09-08 04:29:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071603, 572507, 47483, '<td valign="top">this challenge saw so many good photos that even at 63rd place my mouth is open with awe. Wonderful picture in every respect.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-09-08 18:53:04.</i></td>', 'this challenge saw so many good photos that even at 63rd place my mouth is open with awe. Wonderful picture in every respect.', '2007-09-08 04:32:31.000000', '2007-09-08 19:53:04.000000', 0),
(4071604, 579210, 30861, '<td valign="top">It''s quite liberating, isn''t it, to open up and work the bad weather, the harsh times? That''s what I prefer on the Cape, actually; winter over summer anytime for me, given the choice. And as a resident of the Carmel/Monterey area for 4 years in the late 70''s, of necessity I came to love the sullen light of winter and how it transformed the landscape.<br/> <br/>One gets that sense here. Nicely done!</td>', 'It''s quite liberating, isn''t it, to open up and work the bad weather, the harsh times? That''s what I prefer on the Cape, actually; winter over summer anytime for me, given the choice. And as a resident of the Carmel/Monterey area for 4 years in the late 70''s, of necessity I came to love the sullen light of winter and how it transformed the landscape. One gets that sense here. Nicely done!', '2007-09-08 04:32:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071606, 579488, 4517, '<td valign="top">A well deserved 1st ribbon.</td>', 'A well deserved 1st ribbon.', '2007-09-08 04:34:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071607, 572800, 3746, '<td valign="top">No one can fault you for not being consistant.<br/> <br/>I am starting to see genius in these images.</td>', 'No one can fault you for not being consistant. I am starting to see genius in these images.', '2007-09-08 04:34:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071609, 576563, 68035, '<td valign="top">Michelle<br/> <br/>Congratulations on producing a picture that is both poigniant and funny.  A brilliantly composed composite that tells a story <br/> <br/>Sorry it fell agonisingly short of the 6.  It deserved that and much much more<br/> <br/>Brilliant shot<br/> <br/>Jon</td>', 'Michelle Congratulations on producing a picture that is both poigniant and funny.  A brilliantly composed composite that tells a story  Sorry it fell agonisingly short of the 6.  It deserved that and much much more Brilliant shot Jon', '2007-09-08 04:35:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071610, 579514, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is gorgeous, Slippy! HDRI used to positive advantage without being overtly unnatural. How sweet to see such a flawlessly (and apparently lovingly) glorification of such a mundane object. For me, this is by far the best of your images that I can recall seeing. It suggests a new maturity of vision, or it''s at least a glimpse of a side of you that you have not often shared with us. Congrats on top-20!</td>', 'This is gorgeous, Slippy! HDRI used to positive advantage without being overtly unnatural. How sweet to see such a flawlessly (and apparently lovingly) glorification of such a mundane object. For me, this is by far the best of your images that I can recall seeing. It suggests a new maturity of vision, or it''s at least a glimpse of a side of you that you have not often shared with us. Congrats on top-20!', '2007-09-08 04:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4071611, 579836, 30861, '<td valign="top">I remember remarking to myself how CLEAN this image is, when I first viewed it. Well done, and congrats on top 20!</td>', 'I remember remarking to myself how CLEAN this image is, when I first viewed it. Well done, and congrats on top 20!', '2007-09-08 04:36:22.000000', NULL, 0);
