(4079660, 578962, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by annig:</b></div><hr/><i>I''d love to know how you "painted" this in PS  i am just venturing into that device of wonder! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I just selected colors with the color picker and then painted areas of her skin to more or less match the shading in the photo. I might have used the eyedropper on her skin for some of the shades. It helps to do some real life painting first. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by annig:I''d love to know how you "painted" this in PS  i am just venturing into that device of wonder!   I just selected colors with the color picker and then painted areas of her skin to more or less match the shading in the photo. I might have used the eyedropper on her skin for some of the shades. It helps to do some real life painting first. :)', '2007-09-10 23:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4079662, 578962, 50695, '<td valign="top">oh and I varied the brush size, made it smaller for edges. Also, I painted her at full size before I resized it.</td>', 'oh and I varied the brush size, made it smaller for edges. Also, I painted her at full size before I resized it.', '2007-09-10 23:43:16.000000', NULL, 0),
