(4093409, 579641, 69008, '<td valign="top">The subject in the center stands out among a very pleasing and full background in this. The way the brightness fades from center to edge in the image adds a lot to the effect.  The timing and crop or framing is just excellent too.   I am happy to see that it did so well in a free study.</td>', 'The subject in the center stands out among a very pleasing and full background in this. The way the brightness fades from center to edge in the image adds a lot to the effect.  The timing and crop or framing is just excellent too.   I am happy to see that it did so well in a free study.', '2007-09-16 10:47:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4093514, 579010, 67841, '<td valign="top">Adam - yeah, I have to agree with Jeff on this one.  So much so that I didn''t even recognize the portfolio version when browsing through your stuff last week.  I did give this one a 6, but my vote was down mostly because of the extreme obviousness of the valley dodging at first glance.  The more you look at the piece, the less it seems like it was edited &amp; more natural the light along the river appears - that may have been where you got into trouble with voters like me.  That first impression can do you in sometimes!  The other part I may have subtracted for was the blooming highlights on the foreground branch.  <br/> <br/>Sometimes, after I''m done editing a composition, I''ll bring back the original shot to see if mixing it in will reveal some areas where I went too far.  I think this is a good example where you may have found that technique useful as well!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Adam - yeah, I have to agree with Jeff on this one.  So much so that I didn''t even recognize the portfolio version when browsing through your stuff last week.  I did give this one a 6, but my vote was down mostly because of the extreme obviousness of the valley dodging at first glance.  The more you look at the piece, the less it seems like it was edited & more natural the light along the river appears - that may have been where you got into trouble with voters like me.  That first impression can do you in sometimes!  The other part I may have subtracted for was the blooming highlights on the foreground branch.   Sometimes, after I''m done editing a composition, I''ll bring back the original shot to see if mixing it in will reveal some areas where I went too far.  I think this is a good example where you may have found that technique useful as well! ', '2007-09-16 11:56:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4093600, 579329, 70888, '<td valign="top">super sweet shot miss Kelly and congrats on over a 6,im gunna try hard this month to break a 6 too,lol</td>', 'super sweet shot miss Kelly and congrats on over a 6,im gunna try hard this month to break a 6 too,lol', '2007-09-16 12:32:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4094157, 579717, 61651, '<td valign="top">Odd location for such a transport, but that''s the appeal of it.  The edges around the people are noticeable in a way that I don''t think helps the overall image, though - I would have preferred to be left thinking the two were actually there in that setting.</td>', 'Odd location for such a transport, but that''s the appeal of it.  The edges around the people are noticeable in a way that I don''t think helps the overall image, though - I would have preferred to be left thinking the two were actually there in that setting.', '2007-09-16 16:54:15.000000', NULL, 0),
