(4284144, 579889, 28882, '<td valign="top">just saw this and wanted to show you mine that was so similar.  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=440170" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/596/120/440170.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/596/120/440170.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/596/120/440170.jpg"/></a> <br/>They were both free study shots, both received approximately the same score and placement, and up until this comment, received 6 comments each.  weird huh?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-12-02 23:21:11.</i></td>', 'just saw this and wanted to show you mine that was so similar.   They were both free study shots, both received approximately the same score and placement, and up until this comment, received 6 comments each.  weird huh?', '2007-12-02 23:20:07.000000', '2007-12-02 23:21:11.000000', 0),
(4286715, 578954, 22301, '<td valign="top">I like the shot as is but I think for FS entries to score well you need to  get everything spot on and have something of interest that appeals to the most people. I really liked this shot because it looked like it was almost a negative image taken during the day and converted to black and white. If I did anything to it I would have cropped off the bottom like <a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=619468" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>. Don''t worry about the score, they will come, besides it looks like you followed this up with a PB. :)</td>', 'I like the shot as is but I think for FS entries to score well you need to  get everything spot on and have something of interest that appeals to the most people. I really liked this shot because it looked like it was almost a negative image taken during the day and converted to black and white. If I did anything to it I would have cropped off the bottom like this. Don''t worry about the score, they will come, besides it looks like you followed this up with a PB. :)', '2007-12-03 19:49:21.000000', NULL, 0),
